[83.483878, "o", "s = p.read_text().replace('## Known gaps (0.4)\\n\\nNot finished yet; the tests in `tests/` describe the intended behaviour.\\n\\n- revocations are not implemented\\n- implied roles are only expanded one level\\n- re-granting a held role duplicates it\\n- `Roles:` with several roles is read as one role name\\n- sender check compares the raw `From:` header\\n- held/rejected messages get no audit line\\n- `--dry-run` still saves the ACL and moves messages\\n', '## Implementation status\\n\\nThe 0.4 gaps are fixed and covered by `tests/`: revocations, transitive role\\nexpansion, idempotent grants, comma-separated roles, normalized sender checks,\\nheld/rejected auditing, and write-free dry runs. Dry runs simulate changes in\\nmemory so subsequent requests see the same decisions as a real run.\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[83.484447, "o", "s = s.replace('- Sender not delegated: **held**,', '- An explicit SPF, DKIM, or DMARC failure in `Authentication-Results` from\\n  `mx.fernhollow.dev` is **held** for identity verification, even when `From:`\\n  names a delegated sender. Missing authentication results remain compatible\\n  with older form messages; this is not a full mail-authentication verifier.\\n- Sender not delegated: **held**,')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
